<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-cook-mediterranean-marinated-chicken">How to Cook Mediterranean Marinated Chicken?</h2>



<p>In addition to being a quick marinade that only needs 15 minutes, you can cook your Mediterranean marinated chicken any way you like. While grilling is my favorite method for this chicken recipe, I also love roasting it in the oven for a hands-off approach. And when I need a quick sear, I turn to the stovetop.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Below, you&rsquo;ll find my tips and how I use each cooking method.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken.jpg" alt="Marinated Mediterranean chicken on the grill." class="wp-image-81756" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken.jpg"></figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-on-the-grill">On The Grill:</h3>



<p>This is one of my favorite grilled chicken marinade recipes because as soon as the chicken hits the hot grill, the tangy juices lock in the flavors, and you get those beautiful grill marks. Here&rsquo;s how I do it:</p>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Heat Up the Grill:</strong> Start by preheating your grill to a medium-high heat about 425&ndash;450&deg;F (218-232 &deg;C). Give the grates a good scrub to remove any lingering bits from past cooks, then lightly oil them with a paper towel pad dipped in oil. This keeps the chicken from sticking and makes for easy flipping.</p>



<p><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Prep the Chicken:</strong> Take the marinated Mediterranean chicken out of the marinade, letting any extra drip off. Too much marinade can cause flare-ups or uneven cooking, so this step is worth taking the extra time to do it right.</p>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Grill Away:</strong> Place the chicken on the hot grill and close the lid. Grill for 6 to 8 minutes per side. You&rsquo;ll know it&rsquo;s ready to flip when it naturally releases from the grill. If it sticks, give it another minute. Patience here pays off!&nbsp;</p>



<p>Use a digital thermometer to check for doneness; you&rsquo;re aiming for 165&deg;F (74&deg;C) in the thickest part.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 &ndash; Rest and Enjoy:</strong> Once the chicken is grilled, transfer it to a platter, cover it loosely with foil, and let it rest for 5&ndash;7 minutes. This brief pause allows the juices to settle back into the meat, ensuring every bite is juicy and full of Mediterranean flavor.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-in-the-oven">In the Oven:</h3>



<p>When I&rsquo;m in the mood for a more hands-off approach, I let the oven do all the work.</p>



<p>Oven-roasting helps lock in moisture and ensures the meat cooks through gently and evenly, which is something you don&rsquo;t always get with quicker, high-heat methods.</p>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Preheat the Oven:</strong> Heat your oven to 425&deg;F (218&deg;C). This temperature is ideal for roasting chicken because it cooks quickly, helping the chicken stay juicy and flavorful. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper for easy cleanup, or skip the parchment if you prefer a slightly crispier exterior.</p>



<p><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Arrange the Chicken:</strong> Place the chicken breasts on the sheet pan, making sure to let any excess marinade drip off first. This prevents the chicken from steaming and helps it roast to a golden perfection.</p>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Roast:</strong> Bake the chicken for 20 to 22 minutes, rotating the pan halfway through for even cooking. Keep in mind that <strong>the exact timing will depend on the thickness of your chicken</strong>. Check for doneness with a meat thermometer. It should register 165&deg;F (74&deg;C) when inserted in the thickest part of a chicken breast.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 &ndash; Rest and Serve:</strong> Remove the chicken from the oven, cover loosely with foil (or parchment paper), and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade.jpg" alt="Grilled chicken from the top view." class="wp-image-81757" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Mediterranean-grilled-chicken-marinade.jpg"></figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-on-the-stovetop">On the Stovetop:</h3>



<p>I often turn to the stovetop when I want to get a quick sear for lunch or an easy dinner.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Heat Your Skillet:</strong> In a large skillet (10&ndash;12 inch), heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil over medium-high heat. You can also use a cast iron skillet if you prefer.<br>Pro Tip: Wait until the oil is shimmering hot before adding the chicken&mdash;this ensures a flavorful sear and prevents the chicken from sticking.</p>



<p><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Add the Chicken:</strong> Place the marinated chicken breasts into the pan, shaking off any excess marinade first. Avoid overcrowding the pan to give the chicken space to sear properly.</p>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Cook:</strong> Let the chicken cook for about 5 to 7 minutes on each side. If the chicken releases easily when you try to flip it, it&rsquo;s ready; otherwise, let it cook a bit longer to develop that beautiful crust. Use a digital thermometer to check that the thickest part of the chicken reaches 165&deg;F (74&deg;C).</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 &ndash; Rest and Serve:</strong> Transfer the cooked chicken to a plate, cover it with foil, and let it rest for 5-10 minutes to allow the juices to redistribute.</p>
</div>



