<div id="recipe-81750-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-81750-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="81750" data-servings="4"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Ingredients</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="0"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&#8531;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">olive oil</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">lemon zest</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="2"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&#8531;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">lemon juice</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="3"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cloves</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">garlic</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">minced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Dijon mustard</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">fresh oregano</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">chopped or 2 tsp dried plus more as garnish</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="8"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">lbs</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">chicken breasts </span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">boneless &amp; skinless (6-8 oz each) or chicken thighs</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-81750-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-81750-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="81750"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To make the marinade:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">In a large bowl, whisk together &#8531; cup olive oil, 1 teaspoon lemon zest, &#8531; cup lemon juice, 3 cloves of minced garlic, 1 teaspoon Dijon mustard, 1 tablespoon chopped fresh oregano (or 2 teaspoons dried), 1 teaspoon kosher salt, and &frac12; teaspoon black pepper until fully combined.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing how to make the marinade." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/mediterranean-chicken-breast-marinade.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the chicken into the bowl, making sure it&rsquo;s fully coated with the marinade.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Chicken breasts in the marinade." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/easy-mediterranean-chicken-marinade.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Cover with the lid and refrigerate for 15 minutes or up to 30 minutes.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook on the Grill:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-1-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat a gas grill to medium-high heat (about 450&deg;F/232 &deg;C). Clean grill grates and brush lightly with oil.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-1-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Remove chicken from the marinade, letting excess drip off, and place on the grill.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-1-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Grill for 6-8 minutes per side, or until a digital thermometer inserted into the thickest part registers 165&deg;F (74&deg;C)</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-1-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer the now-cooked chicken to a plate, cover with aluminum foil, and let rest for 5-7 minutes before serving.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Grilled Mediterranean chicken from the top view." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Grilled-Greek-chicken.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook in the Oven:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-2-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat oven to 425&deg;F/218&deg;C. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-2-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place chicken breasts on the prepared sheet pan. Bake for 20-22 minutes, or until a digital thermometer registers 165&deg;F (74&deg;C)</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-2-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer the cooked chicken to a plate, cover it with aluminum foil, and let it rest for 5 minutes before slicing and serving.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook on the Stove:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-3-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large skillet (10- or 12-inch cast-iron skillet or grill pan) over medium-high heat.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-3-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Once the oil is hot and shimmering, place chicken breasts in the skillet, making sure not to overcrowd the pan. You may have to cook them in batches.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-3-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Cook, turning once, for 12-15 minutes, or until a digital thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the breast registers 165&deg;F (74&deg;C)</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-81750-step-3-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer the cooked chicken to a plate, cover it with aluminum foil, and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before serving.</div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-81750-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><b>Yields:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> This recipe makes about &#8532; cup of marinade, enough for 2 pounds of chicken breasts, which is ideal for 4 servings. The nutritional information below is calculated per serving.</span></li>
<li><b>Drip off the excess marinade:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Take a moment to let any extra marinade drip off before cooking. This is especially important if you&rsquo;re grilling to prevent flare-ups.</span></li>
<li><b>Storage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Cooked marinated chicken can be stored in the fridge for up to 3 days. You can reheat it in a low-heat oven (300&deg;F/ 149 &deg;C) for 5-10 minutes or until it is warmed through.</span></li>
<li><b>Freezing:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> I do not recommend freezing raw chicken in this marinade. The acid in the lemon juice will continue to break down the chicken (similar to ceviche), leading to a rubbery texture when cooked.</span></li>
</ul></div></div>
